---
// Method + validated results — factsheet style, real walk-forward numbers
// from docs/M4_EDGE_VALIDATION.md. The numbered steps ARE a sequence: this
// is the actual order the system enforces before real money is allowed.
const folds = [
  { layout: "730 / 180", ema: "1.11", bh: "0.87" },
  { layout: "500 / 125", ema: "1.14", bh: "0.97" },
  { layout: "1000 / 250", ema: "1.12", bh: "1.00" },
  { layout: "365 / 90", ema: "1.18", bh: "0.81" },
];
---

<section class="method" id="method">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">The discipline</p>
    <h2>Four gates between an idea and real money</h2>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span class="n mono">01</span>
        <h3>Backtest equals live</h3>
        <p>The signal and cost model are one code path. The paper bot cannot quietly drift from what was tested — an equivalence test enforces it.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n mono">02</span>
        <h3>Validate out-of-sample</h3>
        <p>Parameters are fitted on one window and judged only on the next, walk-forward across nine years. In-sample results count for nothing.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n mono">03</span>
        <h3>Trade on paper, in public</h3>
        <p>A daily serverless run takes the close, decides, and records every decision to a ledger you can inspect. No exceptions, no edits.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n mono">04</span>
        <h3>Hard gates before money</h3>
        <p>Eight-plus weeks of live paper must clear fixed thresholds — Sharpe ≥ 1, drawdown ≤ 25%, profit factor ≥ 1.3, positive net P&amp;L — before any real capital is considered.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="results">
      <h3 class="results-title mono">WALK-FORWARD RESULTS — OUT-OF-SAMPLE SHARPE, BTC/USDT DAILY, 2017–2026</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Fold layout <span class="sub">(train / test bars)</span></th>
            <th scope="col">Strategy</th>
            <th scope="col">Buy &amp; hold</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {folds.map((f) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="mono">{f.layout}</td>
              <td class="mono good">{f.ema}</td>
              <td class="mono">{f.bh}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="footnote">
        Fees of 0.1% plus slippage modelled per side; next-bar-open execution; the strategy
        beat buy &amp; hold on a risk-adjusted basis in every fold layout tested and roughly
        halved the maximum drawdown. Past performance, simulated or live, is not a guide to
        future results.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .method {
    --paper: #f6f5f1;
    --ink: #101d2c;
    --sterling: #0e6e4c;
    --grey: #5c6875;
    --rule: #d9dcd4;
    background: #fffef9;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Public Sans", system-ui, sans-serif;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem; }
  .mono { font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, monospace; }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sterling);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: "Libre Caslon Text", Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.6vw, 2.6rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 3rem;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 4rem;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr));
    gap: 2.2rem 2.5rem;
  }
  .steps .n {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--sterling);
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }
  .steps h3 {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .steps p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--grey);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .results-title {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--sterling);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; max-width: 40rem; }
  th, td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem 0.55rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  thead th {
    font-weight: 600;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  .sub { color: var(--grey); font-weight: 400; }
  .good { color: var(--sterling); font-weight: 500; }
  .footnote {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--grey);
    max-width: 40rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 1.1rem 0 0;
  }
</style>
